---
source: crates/wolf_sema/tests/layout_diagnostics.rs
expression: "render_tc(&format!(\"{GDTR}fn bump(mut x: u64) {{\\n    x += 1\\n}}\\n\\n\\\n             fn main() -> int {{\\n    var d = Gdtr {{ limit: 7, base: 41 }}\\n    \\\n             bump(mut d.base)\\n    d.base as int - 42\\n}}\\n\"))"
---
error[E0819]: `d.base` runs through `base`, a field of the packed struct `Gdtr`, so it cannot be lent
  --> mem:///main.lu:13:14
   |
13 |     bump(mut d.base)
   |              ^^^^^^ a `mut` claim lends its address
   |
   = note: `Gdtr` is `#[repr(c, packed)]`: its fields sit at any byte offset, so a field's address
     need not be aligned for its type ([abi.layout.packed]). A packed field may be read and
     written; to lend one, copy it into a local, lend the local, and write it back.
